    {
      "name": "mcc_percept_ff",
      "comment": "FEEDFORWARD control (mcc_mode>0.5) -- THE CRUX, \u00a71.1. percept = the OBSERVED opponent colour, read directly. The orientation prior K is matched (identical information is available) but is NOT rendered or subtracted -- there is no predictive loop. On an achromatic test the percept is exactly 0: NO contingent aftereffect, for EITHER orientation -- a feedforward classifier cannot fake McCollough. ALIVE / positive-controlled: on a genuinely coloured test this same arm reports the real colour (percept = observed != 0), so its achromatic null is a real null, not a dead arm scoring a perfect floor. Test regions only, once, gated on mcc_enabled>0.5 AND mcc_phase>0.5.",
